A||||19||Jaei Sun||Anyone else waiting for the MINI??||||4||
Z||000000||Jaei Sun||06-17-2001||11:21 PM||||I can't wait till next year, the BMW remake of the classic MINI Cooper will be hitting the US! The more I read about this little wonder the more I want it!  I see this little car in my future replacing my other daily driver very easily.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.miniusa.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miniusa.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||saleenfiero||06-18-2001||12:51 AM||||I sure am not gonna buy one, but they are still cool cars, of course they'll be next years 'fad' car (as the new beetle, PT, t-bird have been), cute though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||06-18-2001||01:11 AM||||I love the idea, I'm soooo glad to see somebody about to release them here again.  I think the originals were cool as hell, just a little underpowered.  Hopefully with some of the modern stuff available for these cars they'll be nice.  Just imagine what you can do with such a tiny car and hmm...an S2000 type motor <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Well, I guess I'd just get the S2000, but the mini is so cool looking.<P>That's the problem with all the cutesy cars of today (new bug, pt cruiser, etc.); I love the body designs of the new beetle and pt cruiser, but for christ's sake...give us the option of some real power.  The new beetle has the turbo...but why not a hopped up VR6; and why not the 24 valve v6 in the pt cruiser.  I would buy either of those cars in an instant if they had some real oomph.  I understand they're supposed to be commuter cars, but there's a market for fast cars smaller than the mustang/viper/corvette cars and some of us actually look for functionality of a car like the pt cruiser as a good thing too.<P>Damn car manufacturers...when will they learn?  I sure hope by the time I get into the business (future auto engineer) my generation won't be such a bunch of asses and demand some real cars!<P>Ok...ranting complete, you may now continue on to your regularly scheduled program <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jaei Sun||06-18-2001||01:17 AM||||I couldn't agree more about the power issue.  The cars you mentioned along with the mini all suffer from the same problem-- engine bay room.  The engine bay for all these cars are on the small cramped side.  Not to say it isn't possible to get bigger, more powerful engines in them.<P>But The Cooper S is supposed to make around 140-160 I believe.  But I bet there will be aftermarket turbos and supercharger kits like mad for these cars.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||06-18-2001||02:16 AM||||I just clicked over to the Mini site.  LOL, I thought I was on some sort of heart monitor at the start of the intro.<P>Hmmm...  do you think they found inspiration from a beer can when they designed the shape of the exhaust tip?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||06-18-2001||09:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>I couldn't agree more about the power issue.  The cars you mentioned along with the mini all suffer from the same problem-- engine bay room.  The engine bay for all these cars are on the small cramped side.  Not to say it isn't possible to get bigger, more powerful engines in them.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep its possible  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>How about a 5 litre alloy V8.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rover12.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rover6_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rover4_1.jpg"> <P>Have been thinking of putting one of these engines in my Fiero as they are pretty cheap in Aus.<P>Back on Minis, there is a Mini panel van that used to kick around my hometown years ago that had a V12 Jag engine in the back of it. Was also a Mini with 2 engines and 4 wheel drive.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||06-18-2001||09:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>But The Cooper S is supposed to make around 140-160 I believe.  But I bet there will be aftermarket turbos and supercharger kits like mad for these cars.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just checked it in my hottest minis collector edition. Shocked me too. The Cooper S puts out 50 BHP at 5000 RPM. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/minipower.jpg"> <P>The car they are comparing it with has a mega dollar twin cam head conversion on the mini engine. <P>Some more stats on the twin cam:<BR>Top Speeds:<BR>1st gear 60mph<BR>2nd gear 94mph<BR>3rd gear 130mph<BR>4th gear 140mph plus (untested to full)<P>An extract from the article:<BR>Peak power however is attained at a reasonable 7800 rpm. Maximum torque comes on at 5400 rpm, and plateaus at 130 lb/ft. On a power-to-weight ratio scale, the 440kg Miniputs out one kilowatt of power for every 2.89 kilos (4.89lbs/hp).  To settle the argument, the Ferrari F40 gets by with merely 3.13kg/Kw!<P>Pretty awesome little machines with some work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I used to have a Cooper S power Mini as a teenager, it was a fun car. Minis are pretty common in Aus and pretty popular too.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||06-18-2001||10:39 AM||||If you guys want to have a good laugh read last months road and track. They enter a Austin Mini in a classic car rally against such stiff competion as Cobras, Ferrari's, Jags, etc. It's a really good read about the "little car that could". It's really too bad they can't release it at a lower cost to make it available to the masses. The last price estimate I read had it coming at 35,000 US.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||06-18-2001||10:50 AM||||someone here at work has an Austin Mini for sale, frame off restore, $5k<P>  thing that surprized me the most when I saw it in the lot, he has two RIT (Rochester Institute of Technology) commuter student parking permits in the back window.<P> I cant believe he drove it to RIT for two years, and it didnt end up on the roof of a dorm building, in the middle of a lecture hall, or at the bottom of the swimming pool.||||reg||1
