Z||000011||Steve Normington||06-18-2001||04:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beer_stud_21:<BR><B>All I want to know is like when I first got interested in a fiero... WILL I FIT?  I'm pushing 6'7".</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If the interior is the same as the earlier Mini's, yes. I've seen linebacker looking dudes fit in Minis with no problem.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||85SE||06-18-2001||10:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Most reports on the NEw mini say it's sort of like the old mini ..but not quite<P>And am I the only one who caught on to the fact that it has a neon motor in it???<P>Strange but true<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Jonathan...My understanding is that it has the 1.8 lt motor from the BMW family for motivation, and the S model will get the supercharged 1.8 lt.  I was at the Canadian International Auto Show in February where the new Mini was making its only Canadian appearance.  They told me that the Cooper would be about $25K Canadian and the S would come in somewhere around $30K or so.  I think it's an awesome car.  I can't wait until they're widely available.  Serve me up an S please :-)...<P>Andrew<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tina||06-18-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>Not to say it isn't possible to get bigger, more powerful engines in them.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dont't know about the rest of them, but in case of the "Mini" the problem could be the taxes.<P>The more cubic inches you got in germany, the more taxes you pay.<BR>The Mercedes Kompressor is another good example, how german car makers are trying to get around this problem. <P>Tina<BR>BTW wonder if their ever going to bring the<BR>Isetta back?||||reg||1
Z||000014||Robert||06-18-2001||11:31 PM||||I’ve got a Mini Cooper story from way back.<BR>Back in I think 1966 I owned a Datsun 1600 roster.  I was screaming along Highway 1 near Santa Cruz when I look in my rear view mirror and see this little car catching up with me.  Try as I might, I could not stop this little car from pulling along side of me.  I look over to the left and there is a Mini Cooper with 4 guys in suits, sitting very straight and enjoying the ride.  They pass me and dive into the next turn.  All I ever saw of them again was the taillights.  Just put me to shame.  At the time I was a 17 years old motorcycle racer (TT, road race, and short track), but I was never shut down like the Mini did to me that day.  I will never forget that.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||06-18-2001||11:47 PM||||I have a copy of autonews right here, it's an industry publication. They say the motor is out of the neon, then they go on to relate it to the Jeep- chevy joint use of the 2.8<P><BR>I will scan it for you guys...could be wrong<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000016||85SE||06-19-2001||05:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>I have a copy of autonews right here, it's an industry publication. They say the motor is out of the neon, then they go on to relate it to the Jeep- chevy joint use of the 2.8<P><BR>I will scan it for you guys...could be wrong<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Jonathan,<P>Not that I didn't believe you, but I went out and looked for more info on the new Mini.  I found this site: <A HREF="http://www.miniworld.co.uk/content/new%20mini/newmini.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miniworld.co.uk/content/new%20mini/newmini.html</A>  that states that the 1.6 lt engine is from the Neon.  Now what I don't understand is which Neon - the Neon has a 2.0 lt engine.  I guess it's a variation on the design.  Would like to see that article though - sounds interesting.<P>Cheers,<BR>Andrew||||reg||7
Z||000017||Nashco||06-20-2001||01:16 AM||||You can make anything fit if you want to, it's all about space maximization and more often than not making a reliable enough motor that serviceability isn't a problem.  Have you ever seen under the hood of a Prowler...don't tell me car companies are afraid to squish things in there <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  One of my favorite teeny car-fast motor cars in widespread use is the TR6/TR7 with Buick/Olds/Pont 215 CI aluminum V8.  I was actually going to put the same motor in my VW, but decided that would be bad if I ruined it out on the trails because it's hard to replace and find parts for.  The TR6 is about the size of an MGB if I'm not mistaken, and the 215 V8 takes up more room than our 2.8s.  The TR6 originally had an I4, so the V8 is quite a squeeze.<P>Oh, and speaking of PT Cruisers and panel vans, has anybody seen the PT Cruiser panel van prototype?  If they released this, I'd buy it in a second...screw the engine, I'd make it fast, but the body is to-die-for...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_PT_Cruiserfront.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PTVAN_copy.JPG"> <P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000018||Slammed Fiero||06-20-2001||01:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85SE:<BR><B> Jonathan,<P>Not that I didn't believe you, but I went out and looked for more info on the new Mini.  I found this site: <A HREF="http://www.miniworld.co.uk/content/new%20mini/newmini.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miniworld.co.uk/content/new%20mini/newmini.html</A>  that states that the 1.6 lt engine is from the Neon.  Now what I don't understand is which Neon - the Neon has a 2.0 lt engine.  I guess it's a variation on the design.  Would like to see that article though - sounds interesting.<P>Cheers,<BR>Andrew</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't get it either , the article is very vague<P>is the neon sold overseas?? with a smaller motor??<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||85SE||06-21-2001||09:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B><BR>is the neon sold overseas?? with a smaller motor??<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I took a quick look around the Chrysler websites.  Neon is 2.0 wherever I looked.  I saw another article <A HREF="http://www.minimania.com/ArticleV.cfm?DisplayID=1042&SCatagory=Factory&DisplayType=New%20Mini&CarType=" TARGET=_blank>http://www.minimania.com/ArticleV.cfm?DisplayID=1042&SCatagory=Factory&DisplayType=New%20Mini&CarType=</A>  that says the engines are being sourced from a Brazillian company in a joint venture between Chrysler, BMW and the Brazil gov't.<P>Go figure.  All I know is that I want one!<BR>Andrew<P>||||reg||1
